WEBVTT

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:24.480
Unseen speaker: ...

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.500
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Sergeant at Arms is directed to make the proclamation.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:56.720
Alfredo Sotto Corpuz: All persons are commanded to keep silent under pain of penalty while the Impeachment Court is in session for the trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:09.480
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Impeachment Trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte is hereby called to order. We shall be led in prayer by Senator-Judge JV Ejercito.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:28.390
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Amon namin mga pangyarihan, lumalapit kami sa iyo nang may pakumbaba. Batid namin na ang karunungan ng tao ay may hangganan. Ngunit ang iyong katotohanan at katarungan ay nanatili magpakailanman.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:29.330
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Sa

00:05:29.520 --> 00:07:25.610
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: pagtupad namin ng aming tungkulin binang mga senator judges, hinihiling namin ang iyong gabay sa lahat ng aming gagawin. Pagkalooban mo, nawa kami ng tapat na puso at malinaw na pag-iisip. Sa buong panahon ng paglilitis na ito, Panginoon, nakikiusap po kami na kayo niyo kami sa landas na makatarungan na may patas na pagtingin sa karapatan ng bawat isa. Dalhin niyo kami sa liwanag pagkat nakapiring ang aming mga mata, hindi man po namin hiningi, ngunit ipinagkatiwala sa aming konstitusyon ang timbangan ng katarungan. Kumiling nawa ito sa karapat-dapat na pagkalooban nito. Nawa ang inyong salita ang maging gabays sa aming paglilingkod at pagdala sa amin sa katotohanan. Kagaya po ng Winika sa Leviticus 19.15, Do not pervert justice, do not show partiality, but judge your neighbor fairly. Lagi po naman tatandaan ang tagubili niyong ito. Amma, anuman ang maging bunga ng paglilitis na ito, hindi nawa itong makita bilang tagumpay ng isa at pagkatalo ng iba, kundi para sa kabubuti ng sambay ng Pilipino. Lahat po ng aming gagawin ay para sa kalulugod mo at hindi para sa kapinabangan ng sino mang tao, mga partido o kanilang mga pansariling interes. Kundi ito'y para sa pagpapatibay ng aming mainstitusyon ng pamalaan at sa pagpapanatili ng tiwala ng mamamayan sa demokrasya ng aming bayan. Bum puso po naming nananalangin na sa lahat ang aming gagawin, lagit-lagi naming kayong pinupuryan. Amen.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:08:21.650
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Senator-Judge Aquino. Senator-Judge Cayetano, Alan. Senator-Judge Cayetano, Pia. Senator-Judge Dela Rosa. Senator-Judge Ejercito. Senator-Judge Estrada. Senator-Judge Go. Senator-Judge Hontiveros. Senator-Judge Lacson. Senator-Judge Lapid. Senator-Judge Legarda. Senator-Judge Marcoleta. Senator-Judge Marcos. Senator-Judge Padilla. Senator-Judge Pangilinan. Senator-Judge Sotto III. Senator-Judge Tulfo, Erwin. Senator-Judge Tulfo, Raffy. Senator-Judge Villanueva. Senator-Judge Villar, Camille. Senator-Judge Villar, Mark. Senator-Judge Zubiri. The Presiding Officer, Senator-Judge Escudero. The Senate President, Senator-Judge Gatchalian.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:26.290
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: With 17 senators present, the Chair declares the presence of a quorum.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:42.500
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: We note the presence of Senator-Judge Bong Go. We have 18. And Senator-Judge Imee Marcos. We have [unclear] senators present.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:45.490
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: If there

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:59.180
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: are no objections, we dispense with the reading of the July 8, 2026 Journal of the Senate sitting as an impeachment court and consider the same as approved.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:05.960
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: The Clerk will please call the case before the impeachment court.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:14.140
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: 2026. In the matter of the impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:47.000
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Sen. Rafi Tulfo is seeking recognition. What is the pleasure of Sen. Judge Rafi Tulfo?

00:09:50.390 --> 00:10:50.570
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Thank you, Presiding Judge Escudero. Short inquiry lang po for the defense, particularly kay Atty. Mark Vinluan. Atty., you know what? During the last hearing, when you delivered a manifestation in reply to the prosecution's statement regarding the fourth article of impeachment, You said, and I quote, The truth of the matter is this. She and her family were threatened, and while her response was unconventional, it was justified. What triggered her response was a question about Operation Romanov, which is the plot to eliminate VP Sara and her family. End of quote. Now, Atty. Bin Luan, this Operation Romanov that you mentioned, Are you referring to the Operation Romanov mentioned by the blogger Princess Maui during the online press conference of BP-SARA?

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:53.990
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yes, Your Honor.

00:10:54.330 --> 00:11:09.200
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Okay. So, the question was raised during the press conference by this Princess Maui, but I did not see her name as a list of defense witnesses in the pre-trial order. So, will you be presenting her as your witness?

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:22.780
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, at this point, it will depend on... What will be established by the prosecution, the defense reserve its right to call or not call any witness depending on the course of the trial.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:29.740
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Oh, I see. Okay. So, in other words, will you also be presenting any other witness to prove this threat or this operation, Romanov?

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:34.070
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yes, Your Honor. That will be part of our evidence in chief.

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:39.890
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: May this court know now? Kung sino-sino itong mga witnesses na inyong i-present? Of course,

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:46.690
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: of course, Your Honor. We are not at liberty to disclose that at this time. Again, it will depend on the course of the time.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:12:04.360
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Your Honors, Presiding Judge, the first time I've heard about this Romanov is during the Maisog Leaders Forum in Davao City. That was on January 28, 2024. Correct me if I'm wrong. It was mentioned by Mayor Baste Duterte.

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:35.670
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: At that time, hindi ko alam anong ibig sabihin ng Romanov at sino mga ito. In fact, ginugil ko yan. Sino itong family Romanov? So napagalaman ko, apparently, they were the ruling family in Russia that was murdered by the Bolsheviks in the night of July 16, 1918. Malapit-lapit na sa anniversary, 108th anniversary. Kasi ano ba tayo ngayon, July 13. Anyway, may relasyon ba ito sa binanggit ni Bastet sa sinabi ni Princess Maui at yung binanggit mo? Nakakarelasyon ba yung tatlo?

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:41.530
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, I have no personal knowledge of what Mayor Bastet said so I cannot comment on that, Your Honor.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:44.610
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: So hindi mo napanood yun? No, Your

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:44.790
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Honor.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:52.520
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Okay. And last question. What did you mean when you said that BP's arrest response was unconventional?

00:12:55.960 --> 00:13:01.820
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, it was a description, Your Honor, of the statements that she made during that press conference.

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:05.190
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Why is it unconventional?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:12.330
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, the basic meaning of the word is, it will explain itself, Your Honor.

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:19.710
Sen. Raffy Tulfo: Okay, that's all, Presiding Judge. Noted and entered into the records.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:28.550
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Yes, what is the pleasure of the Honorable Defensor, one of the members of the panel of prosecutors. You may

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:28.750
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: proceed,

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:28.950
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Sir.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:14:24.330
Lorenz R. Defensor: Thank you, Your Honors. Your Honors, before we proceed, With the examination of our second witness, Your Honors, the prosecution is in receipt of a letter dated July 10, 2026 from NBI Director Melvin A. Matibag requesting that his testimony be scheduled or calendared at the earliest setting considering that the National Bureau of Investigation, Your Honors, has been invited by the Federal Bureau of Investigation. In coordination with the Royal Thai Police for a regional summit on scam center compounds and transnational organized crime. In that regard, Your Honor, the prosecution would like to request that the scheduled testimony of NBI Director Melvin Matibag be scheduled tomorrow after the testimony of our second witness, Atty. Jeremy A. Lotoc.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:31.970
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: After the testimony of your second witness.

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:32.850
Lorenz R. Defensor: Yes, your honors.

00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:36.990
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: But the supposed witness scheduled for tomorrow is Atty.

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:43.390
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Zulaika Lopez for the gentleman's manifestation in the last hearing.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:55.210
Lorenz R. Defensor: That's correct, your honor. After we have dispensed with the testimony of NBI Director Matibag, we can proceed with the schedule of witnesses as provided in the list to the senator judges last week, your honors.

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:59.290
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: To include Captain Belio, if I'm not

00:14:59.290 --> 00:14:59.550
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Mistaken?

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:03.890
Lorenz R. Defensor: Yes, we can proceed with Atty. Lopez and Captain Belio as manifested last week, Your Honors.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:07.450
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: What is the pleasure of Senator Judge Cayetano, Alan?

00:15:08.190 --> 00:17:26.790
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Mr. Presiding Officer, if no one objects, I will not object to having Director Matibag yesterday, but maybe as a caution to government officials, my good friend, Congressman Defensor. I read over the weekend that Director Matibag is writing because he is to be in a convention meeting the FBI next week. So actually, we're going to be here 30 weeks. We have put aside many, many important things. We have put aside many foreign trips, many local trips, whether it's to help dun sa tinamaan ng Nang lindol sa Mindanao or tinatamaan ng baha ngayon because we have to be here two o'clock until matapos tayo every Monday to Wednesday then after the sauna every Tuesday to Wednesday. I find it in bad taste that a bureau head will dictate to us that he's not available next week. I was Secretary of Foreign Affairs. That's why you have undersecretaries. That's why you have deputy director. So, I mean, I admire the patience of the prosecution, no? But even the prosecution, they have a way of timing and laying down the witnesses, eh. So, I don't want later on to say na eh dapat natanong ko muna ito sa unang witness, kaya lang si director matibag inuna dahil ganito o ganyan. I'd like to put that on record and ask my colleagues if that's acceptable to us. At least those who are not in jail or the 21 of us are here. The whole government, nakatutok. We put aside so many important things. And then one witness, who is in the government, who is a bureau head? Will tell us, sorry, but because he has to be with the FBI, siya na yung mauna tomorrow. That might be a bad precedent, Mr. Presiding Officer.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:30.710
Lorenz R. Defensor: May I be allowed to give a

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:31.390
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: reply? The gentleman

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:34.890
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: will please respond to the appoint of Senator-Judge Alan Cayetano.

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:58.650
Lorenz R. Defensor: With due respect to the Honorable... Senator Judge Alan Peter Cayetano, we will always respect the decision of the honorable court. However, we will only be advancing his testimony one day based on the subpoena that we have requested the honorable court. He is scheduled to testify until Wednesday and that we will not disrupt the scheduled list of witnesses. We will simply advance it one day.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:33.740
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Would you respect, Congressman Representative Defensor, I ask That question poignantly last week. If Matibag will be one of your witnesses for this week and you said no. In fact, you corrected Atty. Ligutan when he mentioned Director Matibag as one of your witnesses and instead gave me a list of Lotoc, Zulaika Lopez, and Captain Belio. Matibag was not included. In fact, I don't think we issued a subpoena.

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:53.250
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: For Director Matibag for this week, given your manifestation after you took over, given that you have, as you said, control and supervision over the private, the counsel for the prosecutors. So he's not in your list this week. He's not being advanced for a day, sir.

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:54.990
Lorenz R. Defensor: May I respond, Your Honor? Please

00:18:54.990 --> 00:18:55.110
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: so.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:19:24.970
Lorenz R. Defensor: Your Honor, that's correct. I gave a list of witnesses scheduled for Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday. However, Your Honor, to add, I also added that since NBI Director Matibag has been requested for a subpoena to testify within the week. I also added in my statement that we will inform the Honorable Court which day we can present the Honorable Matibag and I was expecting him to be presented on Wednesday after the testimony of Captain Belinda Bello, Your Honors.

00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:45.410
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: I confirm that but the situation is Given the one-witness-per-day rule that we supposedly have under the rules of court, no subpoena has yet been issued to Director Matibag to appear this week. Can the Clerk of Court kindly confirm that for us on the record?

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:50.000
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: No subpoena has been issued for NBI Director Matibag.

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:50.400
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: May I

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:55.140
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: respond, Your Honor? Senator Judge Alan Cayetano is recognized.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:35.150
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: My statement and my question to the court is not really addressed to the prosecution. You will have to do the best you can to represent what you're fighting for. So I commend you for adjusting. But my recollection is because I'm also waiting for his testimony. And my recollection last week is that we will not see him this week. And I think 11 days. 11 days ang sa article na to. So we're on day 4. So kung hindi siya pwedeng next week, that's day 7, 8, 9.

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:49.300
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Again, I don't want to dictate sa prosecution or ano. But to suddenly say na tomorrow na siya. When I'm preparing for our oral argument tomorrow and the other witnesses, it's a

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:55.740
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: little bit, it's a small inconvenience for today. But I hope it doesn't become a rule, especially for a bureau head.

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:13.170
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: I mean, if no one else objects, but if someone objects, I don't think it's really a good rule. You know, rules are important. I'll have to keep, you say technicalities, and no, rules are important. So even yung notice, we agreed on, siding officer, three day ba? Five day notice?

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:17.290
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Five days for witnesses not mentioned in the pre-trial order. And

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.790
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: then three days kapag ka...

00:21:19.350 --> 00:21:24.530
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Three days given the fact that we will be announcing the witnesses for the following week on the last day.

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:33.570
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Anyway, I said my piece but I hope we will not be able to move faster if we have to accommodate the witnesses especially if they're in government.

00:21:34.010 --> 00:21:34.990
Lorenz R. Defensor: May I add something,

00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:42.970
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Your Honor? Before the Honorable Defensor, the Presiding Officer would like to hear from the Council for the Respondents. Atty. Vinlun, what say you?

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:51.200
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yes, Your Honor. We would have to oppose. On the basis of the following, number one, it will be in violation, your honor, of the impeachment

00:21:51.200 --> 00:22:12.900
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: court's directive that was given last week insofar as the identities of the witnesses and as well as the order of the presentation. Number two, your honor, it will be again as mentioned by Senator Judge Cayetano, a violation of the five-day notice rule since while he was subpoenaed the week before, your honor, we are learning that

00:22:12.900 --> 00:23:03.230
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: he will be presented this week. The five-day notice will not be observed. Number three, the prosecution cannot compel also the defense and this impeachment court to present witnesses according to their schedule, considering also that these witnesses have already been identified and determined. Of course, it will be a violation of the basic tenets of fair play. And to join again the manifestation of Senator Judge Caytana, it will set a bad precedent. And so far, surprise witnesses will be allowed at any point of the proceedings. Number five would be, it will also violate our right to cross-examine intelligently. We have done our best to prepare for

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:04.690
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: their witnesses. However,

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:18.930
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: these last-minute changes really affect the preparation involved, Your Honor. And insofar as laying down the case that we want to establish and finally if there are violations of these proceeding rights there will be a violation of a

00:23:18.930 --> 00:23:27.830
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: procedural due process which of course can give way to another ground to further delay the proceedings moreover your honor

00:23:27.830 --> 00:23:38.070
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: um we If the prosecution would also allow, can we also get a copy, Your Honor, of that invitation? And may we inquire of the prosecution

00:23:38.070 --> 00:23:48.650
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: if the particular travel authority has already been made? Because, Your Honor, we received information as well that

00:23:48.650 --> 00:24:16.040
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: the FBI had already conducted a summit, a regional summit of some sort, but it was conducted of June. In June of, in other words, last month, Your Honor, also in Bangkok, Thailand. So, we would have to, again, manifest and we would have to study, Your Honor, the invitation and counter-check and do the proper verification as well. So that, if

00:24:16.040 --> 00:24:23.720
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: it is indeed viable, then we would understand, Your Honor, why it has to be attended to by Director Matiba, Your Honor.

00:24:24.030 --> 00:24:27.770
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Um, Senate President Gatchalian, recognized. You may proceed, sir.

00:24:27.870 --> 00:25:44.360
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Thank you, thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. Sinusuportahan ko po yung statement ni Senator Judge Allen Cayetano. Dahil hindi lang naman po yung councils ng prosecution at defense na naghahanda. Pati mo mga senator judges naghahanda rin. At sa totoo lang itong weekend, marami rin sa ating mga senator judges ay pinag-aaralan kung ano yung kanilang maitatanong sa mga testigong ihaharap ngayong linggo. Marami po ay pinag-aaralan po yung mga ebedensyang inupload na para po sa ating mga senator judges. At hindi po ito konting ebedensya, pinag-uusapan po natin dito. Libo-libong mga papel at libo-libong mga ebedensya. Kung bigla pong may isisingit na testigo, hindi ho rin makakahanda po yung ating mga senator judges sa kanilang pagtatanong at hindi rin ho nilang mababasa yung mga dokumento at ebidensya na nakakabit ho doon sa testigong iharap. Kaya napakahirap naman po na naghahanda ho tayo pero biglang may mga ganitong supresya na hindi ho natin paghahandaan at hindi naman ho yan magiging maayos at For the

00:25:44.360 --> 00:25:50.960
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: record, Chair would like to confirm the statement of the Honorable Defensor, I will quote,

00:26:10.800 --> 00:26:42.320
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: We'll take for both parties. With the permission of Senators, Senator Judge Cayetano and the Senate President, may we defer our ruling on this matter and ask the Council for the Prosecution to submit to us the letter given to you by Director Matibag for us to be able to look at it. Copy furnished, of course, the Council for the Respondent so that we can adequately go over it. And hopefully come up with a ruling before the day is over.

00:26:42.860 --> 00:26:44.080
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Would that be possible?

00:26:44.220 --> 00:26:46.160
Lorenz R. Defensor: We will submit the letter. Thank you, Your Honor.

00:26:46.300 --> 00:26:51.900
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: So, we shall do it that way. Kindly furnish a copy to counsel for the respondents as well for their review.

00:26:52.140 --> 00:27:02.600
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yes, Your Honor. Your Honor, if the travel authority is also available, if we can ask for a copy.

00:27:02.840 --> 00:27:05.060
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Travel authority, if it's already issued.

00:27:05.160 --> 00:27:14.820
Lorenz R. Defensor: Yes, of course. Kindly furnish us that as well. Your Honors, we will submit in good faith whatever the prosecution has received from Director Matibag, Your Honor.

00:27:14.820 --> 00:27:29.980
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: As well as kindly communicate with him, if possible, if he already has a travel authority for the same, so that we could evaluate it based on what you have. We cannot evaluate it based on what you don't have. So we will presume if you don't have it, it's not yet there.

00:27:30.150 --> 00:27:47.770
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, one last addition. Considering that there's a if and when they provide the travel authority, I understand, Your Honor, that one of the requirements is also the official invitation from the foreign body. So if they can also provide that, Your Honor, so that we can do a full review of this matter.

00:27:47.850 --> 00:27:55.730
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Atty. Vinluan, it's not really for the full review of the counsel for the prosecution but rather for this court's evaluation whether or not to allow the motion of the counsel.

