Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Well, Your Honor, if If the second highest official of the land, sinabi yan, hindi ho biro yan. Medyo mabigat ho yan. At yung pagkasabi pa niya na may kasamang galit at mga pagmumura. We took it very seriously, Honor.

02:19:11.170 --> 02:19:31.950
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Alright, I have a question for the defense. Sa lahat ng mga sagot ninyo, Atty. Vin Luan, parang hindi ko nakita na tinanggi ng inyong kliyente o ng depensa. Na may nakausap ang vice-presidente na tao para gawin yung mga bagay na ito. Tama ba? Wala ito sa mga sagot ninyo? We deny

02:19:31.950 --> 02:19:32.610
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: that, Your Honor.

02:19:32.890 --> 02:19:33.830
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: You deny?

02:19:34.350 --> 02:19:39.590
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: That is not accurate, Your Honor, and we will present evidence or counter-evidence. Okay,

02:19:39.710 --> 02:19:49.970
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: so let me clarify. Sa lahat ng sagot ninyo so far, hindi pa ninyo tinatanggi ito, pero in your time presenting evidence, you will deny?

02:20:09.480 --> 02:20:17.240
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Ang nabanggit doon ay freedom of expression. Was there an exact statement there na hindi totoo?

02:20:22.670 --> 02:20:23.110
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: We

02:20:23.110 --> 02:20:27.290
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: maintain our position that we denied it, Your Honor. It is there in our answer.

02:20:47.840 --> 02:20:50.100
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: General denial and there were also specific denials.

02:20:50.140 --> 02:20:58.860
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Okay. We'll take a look, Mr. Presiding Officer. Hanapin natin ito. And if I may come back to this once we take a look at the records, Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:20:59.660 --> 02:21:13.600
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: The gentleman may do so at the appropriate time. With the permission of Senator Judge Erwin Tulfo, since nakatayo na po si Senator Judge Ejercito, ang papaunahin ko ng bumuna siya. Senator Judge Tulfo, rather Ejercito is recognized. You have two minutes, sir.

02:21:14.210 --> 02:21:15.690
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:21:18.910 --> 02:21:35.650
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: May we know if the NBI has the authority to issue subpoena against impeachable officials? Kasi kanina po sa mga pinresent kanina, subpoena po ang inyong pinadala sa Vice President instead of a mere invitation. Yan lang po. Clarify ko lang po.

02:21:37.790 --> 02:21:55.950
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Yes, Your Honor. Under Republic Act 10867, the NBI has authority to issue subpoena. As a matter of fact, the case involving the Vice President falls under Section 5, Paragraph G, which the NBI has primary jurisdiction to undertake investigation, Your Honor.

02:21:57.760 --> 02:22:16.050
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Likewise, for the information, may we know what constitutes a grave threat that will prompt the NBI to conduct an investigation as compared to a light threat? What are the elements that are needed to be present to be considered a grave threat.

02:22:16.530 --> 02:22:40.900
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Well, for grave threat, Your Honor, if naalala ko siya, if a person threatens another person with the infliction upon the latter's person, property, or honor, or that of the latter's family with a wrong Atty. Giorgio R. Or

02:22:40.900 --> 02:23:07.870
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: with any wrong, amounting to a crime, if that threat is with condition or without condition or with monetary consideration, yun po yung kabuan sa grave threat.

02:23:10.830 --> 02:23:13.640
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: May kondisyon? Or walang kondisyon?

02:23:13.640 --> 02:23:17.200
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: The crime of grave threat, Your Honor, can be committed with or without condition. With or without

02:23:17.200 --> 02:23:17.560
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: condition.

02:23:19.860 --> 02:23:41.740
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: So as an investigator, have you ever investigated and filed a complaint for grave threats apart from this one? Again, Your Honor? As an investigator, have you filed any case or investigated and filed a case for grave threats against anyone aside from this one, excluding this one?

02:23:42.330 --> 02:23:42.690
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: I

02:23:42.690 --> 02:23:51.090
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: think me, nag-start po kasi ako as counter-terrorism and then organized crime group and then cybercrime.

02:23:53.430 --> 02:23:59.910
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Wala akong maalala, Your Honor, kundi ito lang. I mean, so far as my being in the NBI is concerned, Your Honor.

02:24:00.610 --> 02:24:07.610
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Ah, so ito lamang yung ano, ito pala yung kaso na naimbestigahan niyo concerning greed threats, yun o?

02:24:08.100 --> 02:24:38.620
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: I think yung iba, may mga na-investigahan, Your Honor. Pero again, sabi ko, yung sa sarili ko po, yung experience ko from counter-terrorism hanggang sa Organized Transnational Crime Group hanggang sa Cybercrime Division, ang naalala ko lang, Your Honor, kasi matagal na ho yun eh, kung ano yung nasa record, I think itong great threats na to is, pag hindi first time, Atty. Dung ko lang na-experience.

02:24:39.100 --> 02:24:44.520
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: Gano'ng katagal kayong parte nitong Cybercrime Division? Bukay na

02:24:44.520 --> 02:25:04.570
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: lipat? Since 2018, Your Honor. Nagsimula ako bilang Investigation Agent. And then 2022, I was designated as Chief of the Digital Forensic Laboratory Division. And then 2023, designated as Chief of the Cybercrime Division, Sir.

02:25:04.970 --> 02:25:12.250
Sen. Joseph Victor “JV” Ejercito: So, more than five years kayong nandito sa Cybercrime Division ng NBA? Opo. That's all, Mr. Presiding Officer. Thank you.

02:25:12.670 --> 02:25:19.330
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Erick Soto. Senator Judge Tulfo Irwin is recognized. You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed when you're ready.

02:25:22.280 --> 02:26:10.210
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Mr. President or Presiding Officer. I'd like to direct my clarificatory question to the witness on the stand, Mr. Presiding Officer. Atty. Jeremy Lontoc, What findings, if any, convince the NBI the motive of the respondent to kill the President and two other people? Meron pong bang kayong nakitang motibo? Kasi maaari pong sabihin lang nung isang tao sa sobrang galit niya. Napag-usapan na po kanina yan, di ba? Spur of the moment. Pero did you find any motive? Bakit niya po gagawing patayin ang Pangulo?

02:26:11.020 --> 02:26:26.270
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Yes, Your Honor. As I've said before, when we take into consideration all the facts and circumstances surrounding that issue, nagkaroon ng hindi magandang relasyon yung dalawa.

02:26:29.580 --> 02:26:33.620
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Nagbato na ang vicepresidente ng mga salitang mabibigat laban sa presidente.

02:26:35.210 --> 02:27:09.650
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Pinapakita doon sa October 18 na toxic na nga yung relationship nila. Galit na galit si Sarah dahil sinasabi ng vicepresidente is politically motivated yung pag-attack sa kanya. And then at the same time, pinagtutulungan siya ng buong gobyerno. So, then na-trigger ho yun, if my memory serves me right, nung incident nangyari noong 23 November 2024.

02:27:11.060 --> 02:27:24.680
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: So parang nagpatong-patong na siya, convolution ng iba't ibang issue. So nakita ho namin, talagang galit ang Vice President sa Presidente.

02:27:24.680 --> 02:27:51.940
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Okay, so you saw that the Vice President is very angry, right? Galit po siya. Did the investigation uncover any evidence that the respondent had taken steps to carry out these threats or these statements that she made in public and online? Did you have or did you uncover any evidence?

02:27:54.000 --> 02:28:44.820
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Your Honor, insofar as the Cybercrime Division is concerned, we focused on the investigation on the alleged grave threats and inciting to sedition. Ngayon, pagdating doon whether or not merong na-execute na o may inutusan, I think ang makakasagot po niyan, Your Honor, 'yung aming Director, kasi sa kanya po 'yung pool ng information. But at the same time, 'yung jurisdiction na 'yan, nasa Intelligence Service po namin. Kami ho, nasa Investigation Service. So insofar as the NBI Cybercrime Division is concerned at that time, naka-focus po kami sa grave threats and inciting to sedition. But insofar as whether meron na bang in-engage ang Vice President, jurisdiction ho 'yan ng aming Intelligence Service, and maybe ang makakasagot niyan 'yung aming Director kasi siya po 'yung—

02:28:44.820 --> 02:28:49.740
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: answer that because he is the recipient of a pool of information from different—

02:28:51.290 --> 02:28:51.890
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: You

02:28:51.890 --> 02:29:01.500
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: mean inciting to sedition will be answered by the director, is that correct? Kasi parang hindi po natalakay kanina in inciting to sedition, is it?

02:29:01.780 --> 02:29:50.000
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Well, Your Honor, inciting to sedition, in our investigation, we were able to establish that those utterances from 18 October 2024, November 23, 2024, and other facts and circumstances, even the November 26, 2024, we believed that those utterances have a tendency, Your Honor, to stir up the people, to go against the government, to disturb the peace of the community, and to undermine public safety and public order. I think those are the elements of inciting to sedition, Your Honor.

02:29:50.000 --> 02:30:04.600
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: I have two questions, Mr. Presiding Officer. So you're saying they're intertwined: killing the President and then inciting the people to revolt against the government? They're intertwined, is that what you're saying?

02:30:04.600 --> 02:30:05.760
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Based on our findings.

02:30:05.760 --> 02:30:05.840
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Based on your findings.

02:30:05.840 --> 02:30:28.360
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: What could be the motive of the vice president inciting people to sedition, to revolt against the government, when in fact she will be the next president of the republic? She's been saying and everybody knows and she's been claiming. Why do you think? Did you look deeper? Why incite to sedition?

02:30:29.930 --> 02:30:40.570
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: In fact, you're the vice president. Usually, in our country, usually, Mr. Witness, the vice president would run for presidency. What could be the motive?

02:30:41.510 --> 02:30:57.440
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Well, Your Honor, what we have established is the fact that the relationship between the two were already hostile. And what we established is the fact that the vice president has committed great threats and inciting to sedition.

02:30:58.960 --> 02:31:06.970
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: That is our focus, Your Honor. Insofar as the deeper motive, I have

02:31:06.970 --> 02:31:09.410
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: no personal knowledge. All

02:31:09.410 --> 02:31:29.550
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: right. Well, I'm running out of time. Can you identify the strongest piece of evidence which you relied in deciding to file these cases before the Department of Justice? And what is the status of this case, Mr. Witness?

02:31:30.450 --> 02:32:08.990
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Well, Your Honor, the piece of evidence that we attached or we incorporated in our investigation is sufficient and has satisfied the requirements of the quantum of evidence required which is prima facie evidence. With reasonable certainty of conviction, and the fact, Your Honor, that the Department of Justice has issued certification stating that your referral, your transmittal, has complied all the elements of the crime charge and therefore good for preliminary investigation.

02:32:09.450 --> 02:32:13.770
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: What is the status of the case, Mr. Witness? It's ongoing, Your Honor,

02:32:13.850 --> 02:32:18.560
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: if I remember correctly. It's ongoing, Your Honor.

02:32:19.990 --> 02:32:22.690
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: One very, very quick question, Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:32:22.810 --> 02:32:24.030
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Do you

02:32:24.030 --> 02:32:29.170
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: think at this point you have an airtight case against the respondent? I

02:32:29.170 --> 02:32:44.330
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: believe so, yes, Your Honor. Otherwise, the Department of Justice would not issue a certification stating to the effect na kompleto ang elements namin, na nakuha namin yung requirement, at ready na siya for preliminary investigation.

02:32:44.790 --> 02:32:46.990
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Mr. Witness. Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:32:47.330 --> 02:32:54.730
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Tulfo. Senator Judge Ontiveros, Senator Judge Villanueva, and thereafter, we pause for a 10-minute break.

02:32:58.020 --> 02:32:58.420
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: You

02:32:58.420 --> 02:32:59.680
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: may proceed, ma'am. You have two minutes.

02:33:00.560 --> 02:33:02.180
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:33:04.100 --> 02:33:05.180
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Atty. Lotoc?

02:33:05.220 --> 02:33:06.220
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Yes, Your Honor.

02:33:08.500 --> 02:33:21.360
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: In the affidavit of investigation dated February 10, 2025, the NBI recommended that grave threats and inciting to sedition be filed against

02:33:21.360 --> 02:33:33.470
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: the vice president. Could it be due to those cases that were just brought out of emotion or there was an intense trigger that led to that?

02:33:35.280 --> 02:33:44.790
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: I don't think, Your Honor, kasi wala naman sa elements ng grave threats yung situation na iyon.

02:33:46.360 --> 02:34:03.450
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: As long as we were able to satisfy the elements for grave threats, Your Honor, and when the Department of Justice certifies na kumpleto yung elemento doon,

02:34:07.620 --> 02:34:15.650
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: No, Your Honor. Hindi ho yan mag-matter dun sa findings namin.

02:34:16.190 --> 02:34:26.970
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: At yung sinabi po ninyong elements of grave threats, yun po yung apat na inanumerate nyo kanina. Ano pong elements of grave threats?

02:34:27.150 --> 02:34:35.350
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Yes, Your Honor. Number one, that a person threatened to inflict another person.

02:34:37.820 --> 02:34:59.100
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: On the latter's person, owner of property, or that of the latter's family with any wrong. That's the first element. The second element, that wrong amounts to a crime. Then the third element is my demand for money or my condition in imposed.

02:35:02.190 --> 02:35:31.350
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: In our investigation, mayroon hong tatlong acts para makumit yung great threats. Base doon sa tatlong elements na sinabi ko, the offender have complied with the threat na sinabi niya, the offender hindi niya na comply yung threat na sinabi niya or yung pangatlong act, yung walang condition yung threat na yon.

02:35:32.720 --> 02:35:58.700
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Two times you mentioned the word condition, Atty. Lotoc. I will ask that later. In DOJ, there is a criteria of reasonable certainty of conviction before filing a case. Yes, Atty. In NBI, what is the procedure you follow before recommending a case?

02:35:59.430 --> 02:36:23.200
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Well, sinusunog din ho namin yung quantum of evidence na prima facie evidence with reasonable certainty of conviction. Kaya ho, kung makikita niyo yung yung pong aming processes o yung phases, yung pang last po niya is legal evaluation. Meaning, pag meron na ho kaming conclusion bago ho namin ito i-submit sa Department of Justice, We have

02:36:23.200 --> 02:36:35.480
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: a referral from the legal division. We are helping our legal experts. They are the ones evaluating. They will qualify if the requirements are satisfied

02:36:35.480 --> 02:36:42.240
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: and if they can be submitted to the Department of Justice for purposes of preliminary investigation, ma'am.

02:36:42.640 --> 02:36:46.920
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Thank you, Atty. No matter how you approximate it.

02:36:50.930 --> 02:36:51.490
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Yes,

02:36:51.770 --> 02:37:02.930
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Your Honor. And that is on the basis of our cherished principle, the two-pillar rule in investigation, thoroughness and legality, Your Honor.

02:37:03.490 --> 02:37:04.950
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: All right. Salamat po.

02:37:06.530 --> 02:37:18.950
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Eto, in principle, kailangan po ba ng patunay na may Kinoontratang asasin para maituring na grave threats ang mga sinabi.

02:37:19.670 --> 02:37:25.010
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Well, Your Honor, in so far as the crime of grave threat is concerned, hindi po iyon kailangan.

02:37:25.310 --> 02:37:25.830
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Alright.

02:37:28.250 --> 02:37:42.410
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Speaking of condition, kanina na binanggit niyo dalawang beses. Posible po ba ang grave threats kahit may kondisyon ang banta? Ibig sabihin yung kapag ito nangyari sa akin, ito ay mga gawin mo?

02:37:48.150 --> 02:37:48.710
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Very

02:37:48.710 --> 02:38:29.040
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: much possible, Your Honor. As I have said, grave threats can be committed with or without condition. As a matter of fact, meron akong naalala ng isang case, SPO2 Jamaica versus Atty. Bangot. Ang sabi huto ni SPO2 Jamaica, if I lose my job, I will break your head or I will So it's for us, it's a kind of event-based condition na matitrigger yung execution and threat pag nangyayari yung event. But then when the Supreme Court decide, nag-decided Supreme Court, ito sabi niya, the threat was absolute. So it's

02:38:29.040 --> 02:38:29.580
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: absolute

02:38:29.580 --> 02:38:42.270
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: yung threat, you know, hindi conditional. So parang ganito akin sa situation dito, meron siyang sort of event-based condition. If the event happens, the offender will now be

02:38:42.270 --> 02:38:49.870
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: triggered by the threat that was uttered by the offender, Your Honor. So,

02:38:49.870 --> 02:39:02.010
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: we can say that there is jurisprudence because you can see a correlation in the case of the rule of SC-90PO-2-Jamaca and the case

02:39:02.010 --> 02:39:02.090
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: of

02:39:02.090 --> 02:39:03.990
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: the Vice President. Yes,

02:39:04.010 --> 02:39:04.250
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Your Honor.

02:39:04.430 --> 02:39:16.920
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Alright. Last question, Atty. Lotoc. As an attorney, as a general rule, when can we say that freedom of speech

02:39:16.920 --> 02:39:24.020
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: is beyond free speech and becomes a grave threat or inciting to sedition?

02:39:25.070 --> 02:39:36.760
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Well, we consider the two tests. Number one, I'm not

02:39:38.710 --> 02:39:40.150
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: a big cash owner, but it's like

02:39:43.420 --> 02:39:46.600
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: If I may, Your Honor, just to refer my notes.

02:39:50.340 --> 02:39:51.940
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Kindly turn on the mic. Witness may

02:39:51.940 --> 02:39:52.080
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: do

02:39:52.080 --> 02:39:52.600
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: so. Yes.

02:39:55.790 --> 02:39:57.170
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Thank you. Thank you, Your Honor.

02:40:05.410 --> 02:40:39.760
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: We consider, Your Honor, the clear and present danger rule and the dangerous tendency rule. But among the two, the dangerous tendency rule, meaning if If the speech would have a tendency to create chaos or to create illegal acts, then that should be restricted. Pag may tendency ho na magiging ganon ang resulta.

02:40:39.940 --> 02:40:47.720
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So, huli po, Atty., masasabing bang may parang spectrum? Pwedeng nagsisimula?

02:41:03.850 --> 02:41:04.970
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Thank you

02:41:04.970 --> 02:41:11.790
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: noted and entered into the records senator judge Villanueva you may have you have two minutes sir you may proceed thank

02:41:11.790 --> 02:41:47.140
Sen. Joel Villanueva: you president presiding officer uh just a few questions to our uh witness Mr. Witness, it's been mentioned several times the importance of your investigation that it falls under yung prima facie evidence with reasonable certainty of conviction. And nabanggit niyo po na fulfill po lahat yan, no? Kaya siguro nagkaroon ng first report at second report. Is that correct? Yes, Your Honor. And can you just for the record give us an idea? Ano yung mga boxes that you have to fill in para pumasok po dito?

02:41:50.090 --> 02:41:55.070
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: You mean, Your Honor, the comment of the Department of Justice? Yes,

02:41:55.190 --> 02:42:04.590
Sen. Joel Villanueva: to make it clear that it indeed goes into the Frimafaci evidence with reasonable certainty of conviction.

02:42:05.550 --> 02:42:14.270
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Well, basically, Your Honor, the requirements that the DOJ gave from our point of view were administrative.

02:42:17.320 --> 02:42:49.600
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Hindi ho 'yon 'yung sustansya noong aming affidavit, kasi hindi ho namin binago 'yung affidavit namin. 'Yun pa rin ho 'yon, eh. Ang nakita ho ng DOJ doon, 'yung affidavit of, I think, authentication na kailangan i-attach doon, and others, 'yung TSN, affidavit of transcription. This is, from our point of view, to satisfy the requirements of admissibility. So

02:42:55.330 --> 02:42:57.310
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: it

02:42:57.310 --> 02:43:22.570
Sen. Joel Villanueva: didn't change despite of your fourth stage, the legal evaluation. In that stage of legal evaluation, was it considered, Mr. Witness, what the Vice President mentioned and even some of the defense panel, that it is actually a conditional threat and it appears that the Vice President during the presentation of the video

02:43:30.600 --> 02:43:51.110
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Insofar as the threat against the life of the Vice President, the very reason why we issued a subpoena and sent a letter was for us to have the chance to talk to the Vice President and elicit some information.

02:44:37.550 --> 02:44:43.340
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: But you think—

02:44:43.340 --> 02:44:47.930
Sen. Joel Villanueva: it is important if it is a conditional threat It is also important to look at this aspect.

02:44:49.270 --> 02:44:50.450
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: Yes, Your Honor, I think

02:44:50.450 --> 02:44:50.990
Sen. Joel Villanueva: so. Thank you.

02:44:51.010 --> 02:44:51.790
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Mr. Witness, I would

02:44:51.790 --> 02:44:58.430
Sen. Joel Villanueva: like to understand the standard used by the National Bureau of Investigation. If the so-called assassin is not

02:44:58.430 --> 02:45:21.210
Sen. Joel Villanueva: identified or located, does that automatically mean that the threat is no longer credible or actionable? Or... Does the NBI still consider the statements uttered and the surrounding circumstances and the totality of the evidence before deciding to proceed with further investigation?

02:45:21.690 --> 02:45:35.350
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: No, Your Honor. The threat was absolute. We followed the test of mens rea, Your Honor, in considering whether the threat is true.

02:45:39.270 --> 02:45:59.990
Atty. Jeremy C. Lotoc: We examine the utterances objectively and we interpret the same in light of the circumstances where the utterances was made, the manner in which they were spoken, the person to whom they were addressed, the relationship between the parties and the reactions of the recipients of those utterances, Your Honor.

02:46:01.430 --> 02:46:58.180
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Yes, thank you, Mr. Witness. I have here with me, yung binanggit po niyo sa notes ko, yung four stages, identification, and pag-preserve yung digital evidence, collection of evidence, analysis and attribution, legal evaluation, and then you have the three statements. Binanggit niyo rin, tanggalin ulo niya, toxic relationship, and I always see myself cutting his head. Now you also mentioned the factors considered, delivery manner, literal meaning, nature of the instruction, relationship of the parties, and last but not the least, yung utterances na binanggit niyo doon sa October 18 and November 20. Last question, Director Luntok. Bukod po doon sa authentication ng recordings, maaari niyo po ba sa amin ipaliwanag yung What were the NBI's actions

02:46:58.180 --> 02:47:09.780
Sen. Joel Villanueva: in assessing the statements of the respondents? For example, you mentioned the different things that happened here because the statement you

02:47:09.780 --> 02:47:27.810
